    "diseaseId": "Arthrogryposis multiplex congenita 2, neurogenic type",
    "diseaseAccession": "DI-05199",
    "acronym": "AMC2",
    "description": "A form of arthrogryposis multiplex congenita, a heterogeneous group of disorders characterized by multiple joint contractures resulting, in some cases, from reduced or absent fetal movements. AMC2 is due to a neurogenic defect and is characterized by congenital immobility of the limbs with fixation of multiple joints, and muscle wasting. AMC2 transmission pattern is consistent with autosomal recessive inheritance in several families. Penetrance may be incomplete in females.",
